alice_cust: Hi team — running into a weird streaming issue on Vercel Edge. ReadableStream starts delivering tokens then after ~8-12s the client sees a 401 mid-stream and the stream closes. We only hit this when rotating short-lived auth tokens (our refresh rotates while stream is open). SDK: @redwood/sdk-node@0.14.0, Node 18 on edge runtime. Repro below — anyone seen this?

maya_support: sorry to hear that — can you paste a minimal repro + server logs if possible? also which API route are you calling (/v1/streams or /v1/generate)?

alice_cust: It's calling /v1/streams (server-sent-chunks -> ReadableStream). Minimal client snippet:

```js
// edge handler (vercel edge)
const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/streams', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ model: 'rwd-small', prompt: 'hi' })
});
const reader = res.body.getReader();
while(true){
  const { value, done } = await reader.read();
  if(done) break;
  // process chunk
}
```

Logs we see on client: `200` then a bunch of bytes, then `401` and stream closed. Server logs show: `auth: token invalidated during connection, closing streaming connection (rotated)` at the same time as our refresh.

maya_support: thanks — that helps. two quick questions: are you using automatic token swap mid-request (i.e., issuing a new token while the stream is open)? and can you try pinning the SDK to 0.13.x as a quick check?

alice_cust: yes we refresh tokens via a short-lived lambda that rotates keys and calls the refresh endpoint. pinning to 0.13.5 reproduces less often but still fails ~30% of attempts. current behaviour started after we upgraded to 0.14.0 last month.

jonathan_runtime: pinging eng-runtime — marking this P1 for investigation. quick hypothesis: edge fetch connection is being revalidated against new auth header during reconnect/backoff path, causing the server to treat it as a credential change and tear down the SSE/stream. sdk 0.14.0 introduced a change to reattach auth on reconnects which might be racing with your token swap.

ben_sre: can you share exact timestamps of the 401 events? we want to correlate with our LB logs (we have a known edge case where we close connections when auth headers change mid-stream for safety).

alice_cust: timestamps attached (approx): 1769001208 initial 200/stream open, 1769001217 401 mid-stream. Link to a small HAR-style capture: https://paste.example/har123 (contains redacted headers).

deploy-bot: Deploy 2026-03-17T10:02:12Z — patch/edge-auth-fix queued by jonathan_runtime.

jonathan_runtime: quick repro for us: using local edge simulator + token rotate script we reproduced consistently. root cause: when sdk attempts automatic reconnect with updated Authorization header, the server treats that as session takeover and closes connection. We need to either (A) avoid reattaching new Authorization mid-stream for SSE/ReadableStream, or (B) make server accept token rotation semantics for active streams (requires auth change handshake).

maya_support: short-term workaround for customers: avoid rotating tokens while a stream is open. If you must rotate, create a stable streaming credential (longer TTL) for the streaming session, or re-open a new stream after rotation.

jonathan_runtime: engineering fix: patch ready in branch `fix/stream-auth-rotation` — it disables mid-stream auth rebind for streaming endpoints and falls back to reconnect only after stream end. We plan to release SDK 0.15.0 with this change. you can test the fix by installing:`npm i @redwood/sdk-node@0.15.0-canary.1`

alice_cust: thanks — any ETA for stable release? can we get a hotfix we can pin to?

jonathan_runtime: ETA 24-48h for canary cut, 3-5 days for stable after QA. if you want an immediate workaround we can provide a small patched SDK tarball that forces auth to be sticky for streaming.

ben_sre: we also pushed a transient server-side tolerance change (edge LB) to accept unchanged bearer token for in-flight streams for up to 15s while we roll the SDK fix. that should reduce impact while you test.

alice_cust: installed canary `0.15.0-canary.1` and ran ~20 streams — no 401 mid-stream so far, responses sustained. thanks all.

maya_support: great — marking as resolved for now. please re-open if you see recurrence. we'll follow up with stable release notes + changelog. :tada:

alice_cust: confirmed resolved for our workload, moving token rotation to after stream close as additional guard. appreciate the fast turnaround!
